Overarching: How can a semi-arid state construct a constitutionally constrained AI-governed water allocation architecture that maintains the national water system within a legally defined safe operating space under deep climate and strategic uncertainty?

RQ1 (Balance and Prediction): How can a stochastic dynamic water balance model for a pilot basin (Souss-Massa) incorporate deep climate uncertainty, existing system dynamics baselines, and satellite-derived groundwater intelligence to define a probabilistic safe operating space $\mathcal{S}$?

